# Button variants

## Primary and secondary — light and dark tokens

Primary and secondary buttons use `colorScheme="light" | "dark"` for surface-appropriate styles:

- **Primary light** — green fill (`#00843d`), white text, bright-kelly hover
- **Primary dark** — white fill, dark-green text (`#003619`), bright-kelly hover
- **Secondary light** — green border + text (`#00843d`) on light backgrounds
- **Secondary dark** — white border + text on dark/colored backgrounds

Both CTAs in `TextSection` follow `buttonScheme`: on dark surfaces, primary uses `primary` + `dark`; secondary stays `secondary` + `dark`. Never swap secondary for ghost on dark sections.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — dark section CTAs
<Button variant="primary" colorScheme="dark" href={primaryCtaHref} />
<Button variant="secondary" colorScheme="dark" href={secondaryCtaHref} />

// ❌ BAD — ghost is not a dark-surface secondary substitute
<Button variant="ghost" href={secondaryCtaHref} />
```

## Ghost — photo backgrounds only

`variant="ghost"` is the liquid-glass home-hero secondary (Figma node 1010:1302). Use it only over full-bleed photography with a gradient overlay — e.g. `HeroHomeContent` in `HeroSection` (`full-width` and `rounded` layouts).

Do not use ghost on solid dark section backgrounds; use `secondary` + `colorScheme="dark"` instead.
